                "**Shear**: Sliding force across a section — bolts, rivet joints; resisted by shear strength of the fastener.\n  • 💡 *Simple Explanation*: In plain words, this means how shear works when you look at it in real life.\n  • 🔍 *Real-World Analogy*: Picture this like an everyday system where every part has one specific job to do.\n  • ⚠️ *Common Mistake*: Students often mix this up with related ideas—make sure to mention both *what* it is and *why* it matters.",
